- `HANA-User-Creation-Checklist.md` for onboarding and access setup steps.
- `Technical-User-Control-Guidelines.md` for service account handling and password expiry exceptions.
- `HANA-Security-Review-Checklist.md` for periodic access and policy validation.

## Operational notes

Where the administration tools allow it, administrators can review password policy settings through HANA security or authentication screens rather than relying only on memory or undocumented defaults.[1][4] Password policy and user configuration should also be checked after upgrades, environment changes, or audit findings so that security settings remain aligned with actual business risk.[1][3]

The most useful GitHub content in this area is the kind that turns policy into action. That means combining explanation with concrete checks: who owns the account, what roles were granted, whether password lifetime is appropriate, what happens on expiry, and how the team will handle emergency resets without overexposing access.[5][2][7]
